<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115015" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρῡσοφόρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wearing gold, golden
				ornaments</i> or <i>apparel,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μῆδοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					90
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lycophronid.
					1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.104
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δειρή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					152
				</span></i>
			 (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			epith. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμόνοια,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>BMus.Inscr.</u>
				4.481
			</span></i>*.<i><span class="en">
				471
			</span></i> (Ephes., <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as a priestly title (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσοφορέω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνέδριον χρυσοφόρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ephes.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			 No.<i><span class="en">
				83c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. στρατηγός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BCH</u>
					28.81
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Tralles</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ.</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2929
			</span></i> (ibid.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>carrying gold,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμίονος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>Mith.</u>
					82
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>producing gold,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ χ. γῆς,</span> title of work by
			Teucer Cyzic. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεῦκρος.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσοφόρον, τό,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤλεκτρον</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.83
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
